# clangd configuration for the Super Mario Strikers decompilation.
#
# UnusedIncludes is DISABLED on purpose, and removing this setting is unsafe.
#
# In this codebase an include that a header does not reference itself is
# routinely load-bearing: MWCC GC/2.5 groups weak template instantiations into
# one .text section per declaring header, and that grouping depends on the order
# the headers are preprocessed. Deleting an "unused" include from a header
# therefore moves whole weak-instantiation sections in every dependent
# translation unit, which reorders their .text contribution and changes the
# linked image.
#
# The failure is silent: objdiff and the per-unit match report both keep
# reporting 100%, because the per-function bytes really are unchanged. Only
# `dtk shasum -c config/G4QE01/build.sha1` catches it, and several common ninja
# targets (all_source, report.json, baseline, changes, diff, a single .o) do not
# depend on that check.
#
# An audit on 2026-07-25 found 22 headers whose "unused" include gates weak
# template emission in at least one Matching TU, plus 10 more affecting only
# NonMatching TUs. Accepting clangd's one-click "remove #include directive"
# quickfix on any of them breaks the DOL. The highest-risk ones additionally
# carry an `// IWYU pragma: keep` comment at the include site.
#
# MissingIncludes is disabled for the mirror-image reason: clang-tidy's
# misc-include-cleaner wants to add includes to .cpp files, and adding one in
# the wrong position is the same bug from the other direction.
Diagnostics:
  UnusedIncludes: None
  MissingIncludes: None
